homology implementation, dependency pin, workflow, main branch, or other-session branch is changed.\n\nI read #22's mathematical note at `811210d24b80813a08972ca23f919db015383137`; its strict verification was in progress at that reading. The filtration-level trace budget and multiplicity-correct target `epsilon=o(k q_k)` are retained, without representing pending checks as a certificate.\n\n## Mathematical result\n\nThis continues the owner-delivered Toda-volume construction on the SAME canonical arithmetic source, not a replacement positive metric. For `q=deg chi`, the `2q x 2q` matrix `F_n` consists of **raw full jets of consecutive source orthogonal polynomials** at every root of the original norm polynomial `Pi=conj(chi)(c-iu)chi(c+iu)`, `c=k/2`.\n\nThe note proves:\n\n- `F_n` is invertible by original orthogonality and positivity of `Pi`; its inverse is not claimed uniformly bounded.\n- The exact relation polynomial and norm are constructed by `d_n=F_n^{-1}v_(n+2q)`, `vartheta_n=-d_(n,0)>0`, and `nu_n=omega_n vartheta_n`.\n- The full discrete operator transport is retained: `F_(n+1)=F_n K_n`, with its companion-column determinant and multiplication conjugacy.\n- The two growing Hankel determinants satisfy `B_n/D_n=det F_n/det V`, with the complete raw-derivative factorials in the confluent Vandermonde `V`.\n- The original quotient volume is `(product omega_(n..n+q-1)) det V/det F_n`, for `n=N-q+1`.\n- The auxiliary tilt differentiates this same matrix by a rank-one boundary term. One additional solve calculates the phase `sigma-d_theta log(det G_N)` rather than discarding it.\n- The control numerator is the product of two **positive source-norm gaps**: `Delta_j=||psi Qhat_j-Q_(j+q)||^2=nu_j-omega_(j+q)`, and `epsilon_N^2=Delta_(n-1)Delta_n/(nu_(n-1)omega_N)-phase_N^2`.\n\nAll original `g=2 xi`, arithmetic Taylor units, mass `mu_h^k`, signs, full multiplicities, source relations and e/tau maps remain. The norm-helper algebra `C[S]/chi_1^2` is connected to the genuine conormal depth by the explicit surjections onto `C[S]/chi_2` and `C[S]/chi_1`; it is not substituted for the actual pullback of `I^2`.\n\nThe general Christoffel transformation is classical. The contribution is its explicit confluent arithmetic implementation and its compatibility with the programme's source, control, phase and conormal maps. The fixed width does not by itself supply well-conditioned computation or the required uniform asymptotic estimate.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe public **eight-method exact core** passed fresh normal and `python -O` runs, with identical successful records; both deliberate-failure controls failed. Its exact published blob `53abdeda395040302d1f75c6b09e2ce7cce0d398` matches the locally tested bytes. `VALIDATION.json` records hashes and the execution scope.\n\nThe expanded conversation delivery has twenty passing exact methods in both modes, with both negative controls failing. All 35 manifest entries of the preceding Toda archive verified, and its 24-method checker passed fresh normal and optimized runs. These are finite Gaussian/atomic calibrations, not actual zeta packets, validated arithmetic quadrature, or new Lean certificates. The general assertions have the complete written proofs in `RESEARCH_NOTE.md`.\n\n## Parallel handoff\n\n`HANDOFF.md` gives bounded finite targets using the existing conormal, quotient, trace and support library. This branch handles analytic comparison and finite calculations; #22 and Codex can continue formalization independently. No merge is requested as part of this action, and no global RH/purity claim is made.","created_at":"2026-09-12T22:37:02Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T23:03:15Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"236a82fe7e041b026ea4a5a82f137603c5d79a99","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pulls/24/commits","review_commen